  "source_mechanism": [
    "ScriptedInput::pump posts all due non-resize actions in source order, then a consumed-prefix marker before a synchronous resize when preceding input has not been acknowledged.",
    "Application::handle_event currently acknowledges that marker and immediately reenters pump_replay within the same bounded SDL event drain.",
    "The pending resize changes the native window and posts its size event before the outer loop calls render_frame. The old-size Flat view therefore can never be painted in that catch-up turn.",
    "record_painted_presentation is called only after paint_instrument and successful SDL_RenderFlush. Its omission truthfully reflects absence of that frame; it is not a history deduplication defect."
  ],
  "causality_limit": "The complete retained diagnostics and source establish the omitted-paint mechanism and its match to the observed 1740→2209ms/frame13→14 transition. There is no per-marker timing trace; no specific scheduler, cold-paint or CPU-contention cause is asserted.",
  "proposal": {
    "production_file": "apps/standalone/main.cpp",
    "change": "Within the successful replay_.acknowledge(event) branch, retain eager pump_replay only if last_painted_ exists and matches current workspace, presentation and overlay. Otherwise return to the ordinary render before the existing next-loop pump. Update both marker-branch and run-loop comments.",
    "semantic_comparison_fields": [
      "workspace",
      "presentation",
      "overlay"
    ],
    "excluded_comparison_fields": [
      "window_width",
      "window_height",
      "controls",
