      "normal_operation_and_midi_only_replay": "Marker branch requires a nonempty UI input script; unchanged otherwise.",
      "pure_resize_case": "After at most one initial ordinary paint establishes last_painted_, semantic identity stays equal, preserving eager resize-only draining within the existing 256-event turn budget. The existing two 256-resize acceptance cases must both pass; timeout failure is not acceptable for those cases.",
      "adverse_plan_limit": "Additional ordinary-loop paints are bounded by acknowledged prefix markers, not wall-clock fairness. General expensive semantic/resize mixes retain the existing fixed drain deadline and must never gain an unlimited grace period."
    },
    "guarantee": "If the final semantic view of an acknowledged resize-separated prefix differs from the last actual painted semantic view, that current view receives the ordinary outer-loop paint opportunity at its current size before the next replay prefix is pumped. This does not promise each pure resize or every intermediate non-resize semantic event a separate frame.",
